  "id": "wbx-ef-efm-univ-xd",
  "title": "Universal Economic Fitness Metric",
  "category": "economy",
  "icon": "📊",
  "desc": "The Universal Economic Fitness (UEF) is both a measure of a country’s diversification and ability to produce complex goods on a globally competitive basis. Countries with the highest levels of EF have capabilities to produce a diverse portfolio of products, ability to upgrade into ever-increasing complex goods, tend to have more predictable long-term growth, and to attain good competitive position relative to other countries. Countries with low UEF levels tend to suffer from poverty, low capabilities, less predictable growth, low value-addition, and trouble upgrading and diversifying faster than other countries. The starting data is the COMTRADE list of products and the IMF-BOP list of servi",
